---
description: Animation rules for GSAP, ScrollTrigger, Lenis
globs: ["**/*.tsx", "**/*.ts"]
alwaysApply: false
---

- Animate only `transform` and `opacity`. Never width, height, top, left, margin, box-shadow.
- Register plugins once in `/lib/gsap.ts`. Import gsap from there everywhere.
- Use `useGSAP` with a scope ref. All triggers must clean up on unmount.
- Lenis drives scroll: `lenis.on('scroll', ScrollTrigger.update)`, add lenis.raf to `gsap.ticker`, set `gsap.ticker.lagSmoothing(0)`.
- Call `ScrollTrigger.refresh()` after fonts and images load.
- Never call setState inside scroll or onUpdate handlers. Use refs and direct DOM or canvas writes.
- Pinned sections: use `pin: true`, `scrub: 1` (or `true` for frame sequences), `anticipatePin: 1`.
- Frame sequences: preload into `ImageBitmap`/`Image` array, draw to canvas with `requestAnimationFrame`, size canvas for devicePixelRatio capped at 2.
- Wrap everything in `gsap.matchMedia()`. Under `(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` skip scrubbing, show static end states.
- Easing: slow and soft (`power2.out`, `power3.inOut`). Durations 0.8-1.4s for reveals. This brand is slow living, nothing snappy or bouncy.
- Add `will-change: transform` only on actively animating elements, remove after.
